.TH strip "" "Command"
.SH NAME
strip \- strip symbol table and relocation information from object file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstrip \fIfile ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
strip -- strip symbol table and relocation information from object file
Usage:	strip file ...
.HE
.B strip
rewrites each
.I file
in place, removing its debug table, symbol table, and relocation
information, and marking it as stripped.
This makes the object file smaller, at the cost of the information
a debugger or
.B ld \-r
would need.
.PP
.B strip
copies each
.I file
to a temporary file while stripping it, then copies the result back
over the original; if
.I file
has already been stripped,
.B strip
leaves it unchanged.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B ld
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B strip
complains if a
.I file
cannot be opened, is not in the expected object-file format, or ends
unexpectedly while being read.
If a write error occurs while rewriting
.IR file ,
the stripped copy is left in the temporary file and
.B strip
reports where, so that no data is lost.
.SH NOTES
.B strip
removes its temporary file when interrupted.
